==Extra Stages==
Within the game's code, [[Imminent Disaster]] has five additional stages that are the exact same as those found in [[Here Be Dragons]], minus [[Pilaf Field]]; [[The Gates of Aku|Unleashing the Cats]] has a duplicate of [[Taking the Stage (Insane)]]; [[Congratulations! Mid-Autumn Festival!|Happy Mid-Autumn Festival!]] has two completely empty stages; and [[Santa Claws at Work!|Night 1: Santa Claws at Work]] has a duplicate of [[Harvest Festival]]. All of these extra stages lack an energy cost, XP drop, difficulty, music or drop rewards of any kind.

==Weak Yet Bitter==
The names of [[Weak & Mildly Acidic|sub-chapter 28]] and its stages could be found in the game data for an indeterminate amount of time before they were implemented. The stages' names were no different, but the sub-chapter was originally called '''Weak Yet Bitter''', which was changed to Weak & Mildly Acidic on its release.

==Region Exclusives==
All region-exclusive units and stages (including collab ones) exist in the files of all versions, but with their sprites and assets removed. Some use placeholders for their names and descriptions, but others have official translations.

A notable case of this is [[Nekondo (Special Cat)|Nekondo]]: his [[Punchy Prizefighter|stage]] is translated, but not the unit himself.

